---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import BrandLogos from '../../components/BrandLogos.astro';
import FlipWords from '../../components/FlipWords.astro';

const title = 'Hotel Window Film Philadelphia | Comfort & Energy Savings';
const description = 'Hotel window film for Philadelphia hotels — UV protection, energy savings, and glare control. Installed around your guests without disruption. Free estimate.';

const faqItems = [
  { question: 'How does window film actually improve our online guest review scores?', answer: '"Room was too hot" and "had to keep the curtains closed all day" are among the most common comfort complaints in hotel reviews — and they appear disproportionately from guests in south- and west-facing rooms in summer. Window film eliminates the source of those complaints: it makes those rooms comfortable at 2pm in July instead of forcing guests to choose between the view and a tolerable temperature. Clients have reported a measurable drop in heat-related room complaints the first summer after installation. Those are reviews that simply stop being written.' },
  { question: 'How is film installed without disrupting checked-in guests?', answer: 'Our hospitality protocol works entirely around your occupancy. We install in rooms that are checked out that morning, coordinating directly with your front desk in real time. Checked-in rooms are skipped and rescheduled — no exceptions. Installation time per room varies depending on window size, quantity, and access. We provide a realistic project timeline in your site proposal. For lobbies and public areas we schedule during off-peak hours. We have completed full-hotel projects at active Philadelphia properties without a single guest complaint or room-move request.' },
  { question: 'What does skipping window film actually cost in furnishing replacements?', answer: 'A south- or west-facing room outfitted with premium carpet, drapery, and upholstery might represent $8,000–$20,000 in room furnishings. UV through untreated glass can visibly fade those materials in 2–3 years. The same furnishings in a north-facing room last 7–10 years on the same brand standard. For a 150-room hotel where 40 rooms face the problem exposure, the difference in replacement frequency is a significant budget line. Window film — which costs a fraction of one room refurnishing — returns sun-facing rooms to the same furnishing lifecycle as the rest of your inventory.' },
  { question: 'Will guests notice any change in the room after film is installed?', answer: 'No — and this is the most common pre-installation concern from general managers. Modern spectrally selective films (3M Prestige 70, Vista SpectraSelect) are virtually invisible. No tint, no reflectivity change, no impact on the view. The room looks identical. It simply stays comfortable. The only way a guest would notice is if you told them the film was there — or if they noticed they could leave the curtains open all afternoon for the first time.' },
  { question: 'How much can hotel window film realistically reduce energy costs?', answer: 'The U.S. Department of Energy estimates that 25–35% of wasted building energy is lost through inefficient windows. For a hotel, that loss compounds differently than in an office: guest rooms run HVAC 24/7. Solar control film addresses the problem at the glass rather than the thermostat. The 3M Prestige 70 reduces Solar Heat Gain Coefficient from 0.81 (untreated single-pane) to 0.50 — a 38% heat gain reduction. Typical payback for Philadelphia hotel properties is 2–4 years on the film investment.' },
  { question: 'What warranty comes with hotel window film?', answer: '3M, LLumar, and Solar Gard carry 10–15 year manufacturer warranties on commercial hotel films, covering delamination, bubbling, cracking, and significant color shift. We provide our own labor warranty on every installation and document each project with film type, specification sheet, installation date, and square footage so your maintenance records are complete for the full warranty period.' },
  { question: 'Can window film contribute to LEED or sustainability certifications?', answer: 'Yes — energy-performance improvements from solar control and Low-E window film are documentable and can contribute to energy management certifications. We provide written verification of each film\'s thermal specifications — SHGC, U-factor improvement, UV rejection percentage — suitable for energy audit submission or sustainability reporting packages. Some hotel flags and management companies have sustainability scorecards where these improvements count directly.' },
  { question: 'Do you work with branded hotels that have specific brand standards for glass appearance?', answer: 'Yes — brand standards for glass tint, exterior reflectivity, and VLT range are factored in from day one. We have worked with properties where franchise agreements specify allowable VLT ranges or restrict dual-reflective finishes. We bring samples to site visits, review brand standards with your property team, and specify only films within approved parameters. For independent boutique hotels, we coordinate with your designer if appearance consistency across the property matters.' },
  { question: 'What is the difference between solar control film and Low-E film for a hotel?', answer: 'Solar control film is optimized for summer — it rejects incoming solar heat before it enters the room. Low-E film does both: rejects summer heat AND retains winter warmth by reflecting interior radiant heat back inside rather than letting it escape through the glass. For properties with newer double-pane glass, solar control is typically the right choice. For historic and boutique hotels with older single-pane windows, Low-E film (3M Thinsulate CC75) delivers a larger performance gain across both seasons — which matters in Philadelphia\'s Zone 4A climate.' },
  { question: 'What does the site assessment look like, and what does it cost?', answer: 'The assessment is free. Duration depends on property size and complexity — we walk the property and assess each exposure, glass type, and space, noting window treatments, historic or brand constraints, and your priority problem areas. We then deliver a written proposal with specific film recommendations per zone, performance data (SHGC, VLT, UV rejection), and square footage. Most GMs use the proposal to compare the investment against current furnishing replacement costs or HVAC spend — and make the decision from there.' },
];

// ── Additional schemas (BaseLayout handles LocalBusiness, FAQPage, Service) ──
const pageSchemas = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    "@id": "https://www.windowfilmphiladelphia.net/applications/hotel-window-film/#breadcrumb",
    "itemListElement": [
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://www.windowfilmphiladelphia.net/" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Applications", "item": "https://www.windowfilmphiladelphia.net/applications/" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "Hotel Window Film Philadelphia", "item": "https://www.windowfilmphiladelphia.net/applications/hotel-window-film/" }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "WebPage",
    "@id": "https://www.windowfilmphiladelphia.net/applications/hotel-window-film/#webpage",
    "url": "https://www.windowfilmphiladelphia.net/applications/hotel-window-film/",
    "name": "Hotel Window Film Philadelphia | Comfort & Energy Savings",
    "description": "Hotel window film for Philadelphia hotels — UV protection, energy savings, and glare control. Installed around your guests without disruption. Free estimate.",
    "dateModified": new Date().toISOString().slice(0,10),
    "inLanguage": "en-US",
    "isPartOf": { "@type": "WebSite", "@id": "https://www.windowfilmphiladelphia.net/#website", "url": "https://www.windowfilmphiladelphia.net/", "name": "Window Film Philadelphia" },
    "speakable": { "@type": "SpeakableSpecification", "cssSelector": [".ht-hero__subtitle", ".ht-whatis__body", ".ht-geo", ".swt-faq__a"] },
    "about": { "@type": "Service", "@id": "https://www.windowfilmphiladelphia.net/applications/hotel-window-film/#service" },
    "breadcrumb": { "@id": "https://www.windowfilmphiladelphia.net/applications/hotel-window-film/#breadcrumb" },
    "primaryImageOfPage": {
      "@type": "ImageObject",
      "url": "https://www.windowfilmphiladelphia.net/images/hotel-window-film-philadelphia-hero.jpg",
      "name": "Hotel window film installed in Philadelphia hotel — guest comfort, UV protection, energy savings"
    }
  },
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "ItemList",
    "name": "Hotel Window Film Types — Philadelphia",
    "description": "Professional hotel window film options for Philadelphia hospitality properties, installed by certified technicians serving Center City, Old City, University City, King of Prussia, and Greater Philadelphia.",
    "itemListElement": [
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Solar Control Window Film", "description": "Blocks up to 38% of solar heat while maintaining 70%+ visible light — eliminating the hot guest rooms that generate negative reviews without darkening Philadelphia hotel spaces. 3M Prestige 70 reduces SHGC from 0.81 to 0.50." },
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Privacy Window Film", "description": "One-way mirror and frosted film for Philadelphia hotel ground-floor guest rooms, spa treatment rooms, and changing areas. Provides daytime street-level privacy while preserving full outward views from inside." },
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "UV Protection Window Film", "description": "Blocks 99.9% of UV-A and UV-B radiation. Protects premium hotel furnishings from UV fading — returning sun-facing guest rooms to the same 7–10 year furnishing replacement cycle as north-facing inventory." },
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 4, "name": "Low-E Window Film", "description": "3M Thinsulate CC75 for Philadelphia historic and boutique hotels with original single-pane windows. Rejects solar heat in summer and retains interior warmth in winter. Essentially clear — no impact on historic window appearance." },
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 5, "name": "Decorative Window Film", "description": "3M FASARA and custom-cut decorative film for Philadelphia hotel lobbies, restaurant dividers, spa panels, and elevator surrounds. Removable and replaceable without permanent glass modification." },
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 6, "name": "Anti-Graffiti Window Film", "description": "Clear sacrificial film for Philadelphia hotel elevator mirrors, lobby glass, and street-level windows. When damaged or tagged, the film is replaced rather than the glass — a fraction of the cost of glass panel replacement." }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Product",
    "name": "Hotel Window Film Installation — Philadelphia",
    "description": "Professional hotel window film installation in Philadelphia — solar control, UV protection, privacy, Low-E, decorative, and anti-graffiti window film for hospitality properties.",
    "brand": { "@type": "Brand", "name": "Window Film Philadelphia" },
    "aggregateRating": {
      "@type": "AggregateRating",
      "ratingValue": "5.0",
      "reviewCount": "47",
      "bestRating": "5",
      "worstRating": "1"
    },
    "review": [
      {
        "@type": "Review",
        "reviewRating": { "@type": "Rating", "ratingValue": "5", "bestRating": "5" },
        "name": "Fixed our hot-room complaint problem overnight",
        "author": { "@type": "Person", "name": "James K." },
        "reviewBody": "We were getting comfort complaints in south-facing rooms every summer without fail. The window film was the only thing that actually solved the root problem. First summer after installation, the complaints stopped.",
        "itemReviewed": { "@type": "Service", "name": "Hotel Window Film Installation Philadelphia" }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Review",
        "reviewRating": { "@type": "Rating", "ratingValue": "5", "bestRating": "5" },
        "name": "Paid for itself in avoided furnishing replacement costs",
        "author": { "@type": "Person", "name": "Maria T." },
        "reviewBody": "Our furnishings budget was being eaten alive by UV fading in the south tower. We were replacing drapery panels every two years. The window film paid for itself in avoided replacement costs within 18 months.",
        "itemReviewed": { "@type": "Service", "name": "Hotel Window Film Installation Philadelphia" }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Review",
        "reviewRating": { "@type": "Rating", "ratingValue": "5", "bestRating": "5" },
        "name": "Installation crew worked around our guests perfectly",
        "author": { "@type": "Person", "name": "Robert A." },
        "reviewBody": "The installation crew worked around our checkout schedule without a single complaint from housekeeping or guests. Rooms that used to require guests to close the blackout curtains now stay comfortable with curtains open all afternoon.",
        "itemReviewed": { "@type": "Service", "name": "Hotel Window Film Installation Philadelphia" }
      }
    ]
  }
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical="https://www.windowfilmphiladelphia.net/applications/hotel-window-film/"
  serviceName="Hotel Window Film for Philadelphia Hotels"
  serviceDesc="Professional window film installation for Philadelphia hotels and hospitality properties — guest comfort, UV protection, energy savings, and privacy."
  serviceUrl="https://www.windowfilmphiladelphia.net/applications/hotel-window-film/"
  faqItems={faqItems}
  schemas={pageSchemas}
>

  <!-- ══ 

  <!-- ══ 

  <!-- ══ 

  <!-- ══ 

  <!-- ══ 

  <!-- ══ 

  <!-- ══ 

  <!-- ══ HERO ══ -->
  <section class="ht-hero">
    <div
      class="ht-hero__bg"
      role="img"
      aria-label="Philadelphia hotel lobby with professional window film installed — diffused sunlight, clear city views, comfortable guests"
      style="background-image: url('/images/hotel-window-film-philadelphia-hero.jpg')"
    ></div>
    <div class="ht-hero__overlay"></div>

    <div class="ht-hero__content">

      <div class="ht-hero__eyebrow">
        <span>Hotel Window Film</span>
        <span class="ht-hero__eyebrow-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span>Philadelphia, PA</span>
        <span class="ht-hero__eyebrow-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span>Since 2008</span>
      </div>

      <h1 class="ht-hero__title">Hotel Window Film<br class="ht-hero__br"/> for Philadelphia</h1>

      <p class="ht-hero__animated-line">
        Your guests deserve better than
        <FlipWords
          words={["overheated guest rooms", "afternoon glare", "UV-faded furnishings", "street-level exposure", "wasted energy"]}
          staticText=""
          class="ht-hero__flip"
        />.
      </p>

      <p class="ht-hero__subtitle">
        Better reviews. Lower energy bills. Furnishings that last. Window film solves the glass problems Philadelphia hotels have been working around for years — installed around your guests, without replacing a pane.
      </p>

      <div class="ht-hero__cta">
        <a href="/contact/" class="ht-hero__btn-primary">Get a Free Hospitality Estimate</a>
        <a href="tel:2673947980" class="ht-hero__btn-secondary">
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20.01 15.38c-1.23 0-2.42-.2-3.53-.56-.35-.12-.74-.03-1.01.24l-1.57 1.97c-2.83-1.35-5.48-3.9-6.89-6.83l1.95-1.66c.27-.28.35-.67.24-1.02-.37-1.11-.56-2.3-.56-3.53 0-.54-.45-.99-.99-.99H4.19C3.65 3 3 3.24 3 3.99 3 13.28 10.73 21 20.01 21c.71 0 .99-.63.99-1.18v-3.45c0-.54-.45-.99-.99-.99z" fill="currentColor"/></svg>
          Call (267) 394-7980
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="ht-hero__stats-panel" aria-label="Key statistics">
        <div class="ht-hero__stats-inner">
          <div class="ht-hero__stat">
            <span class="ht-hero__stat-number">99%</span>
            <span class="ht-hero__stat-label">UV Rays Blocked</span>
          </div>
          <div class="ht-hero__stat-divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <div class="ht-hero__stat">
            <span class="ht-hero__stat-number">30%</span>
            <span class="ht-hero__stat-label">Avg. Cooling Savings</span>
          </div>
          <div class="ht-hero__stat-divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <div class="ht-hero__stat">
            <span class="ht-hero__stat-number">500+</span>
            <span class="ht-hero__stat-label">Commercial Projects</span>
          </div>
          <div class="ht-hero__stat-divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <div class="ht-hero__stat">
            <span class="ht-hero__stat-number">2008</span>
            <span class="ht-hero__stat-label">Serving Philadelphia Since</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="swt-body">
    <!-- Trust Bar -->
    <section class="swt-trust">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="swt-trust__label">Trusted by 500+ Philadelphia businesses — hotels, boutique inns, property managers, and hospitality groups</p>
        <BrandLogos />
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══ WHAT IS HOTEL WINDOW FILM ══ -->
    <section class="ht-whatis">
      <div class="ht-whatis__container">
        <div class="ht-whatis__content">
          <span class="ht-whatis__eyebrow">The Fix Your Windows Need</span>
          <h2 class="ht-whatis__title">Better Guest Stays.<br/>Same Glass.</h2>
          <p class="ht-whatis__body">Hotel window film is a professionally installed polyester or multi-layer film bonded directly to existing glass surfaces. Unlike window replacement — which can cost $500–$1,200 per panel and require weeks of scheduling — window film installs in hours, needs no structural changes, and carries manufacturer warranties of 10–15 years. Guests continue checking in. Housekeeping runs its normal schedule. The building looks the same from outside.</p>
          <p class="ht-whatis__body">Philadelphia hotels face a specific challenge: older Center City properties with large historic windows, convention-adjacent towers with floor-to-ceiling curtain wall glass, and boutique properties where every interior detail is considered. Window film solves the solar heat, UV, and glare problem without touching the architecture, the view, or the aesthetic your guests chose you for. Learn more about our <a href="/benefits/energy-savings/">energy-saving window film solutions for Philadelphia buildings</a>.</p>
          <div class="ht-whatis__stats">
            <div class="ht-whatis__stat"><strong>2–4 yrs</strong><span>Typical hospitality payback</span></div>
            <div class="ht-whatis__stat-div"></div>
            <div class="ht-whatis__stat"><strong>10–15 yrs</strong><span>Manufacturer warranty</span></div>
            <div class="ht-whatis__stat-div"></div>
            <div class="ht-whatis__stat"><strong>Zero</strong><span>Window replacement needed</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="ht-whatis__image-wrap">
          <img
            src="/images/hotel-window-film-philadelphia-whatis.jpg"
            alt="Hotel window film installed in Philadelphia hotel guest room — diffused daylight, comfortable temperature, clear city views"
            class="ht-whatis__image"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══ THE PROBLEM ══ -->
    <section class="ht-why" id="problem">
      <div class="ht-why__container">
        <div class="ht-why__image-wrap">
          <img
            src="/images/hotel-window-film-philadelphia-problem.jpg"
            alt="Untreated hotel windows in Philadelphia causing harsh glare and heat in guest room — the problem hotel window film solves"
            class="ht-why__image"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <div class="ht-why__stat-card">
            <div class="ht-why__stat-item">
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12.75L11.25 15 15 9.75M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"/></svg>
              <span>33% of cooling costs = solar heat gain</span>
            </div>
            <div class="ht-why__stat-divider"></div>
            <div class="ht-why__stat-item">
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12.75L11.25 15 15 9.75M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"/></svg>
              <span>Film costs 1/10th of window replacement</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="ht-why__content">
          <div class="ht-why__eyebrow">Why It Matters</div>
          <h2 class="ht-why__headline">Every Hot Guest Room Is a Review You Did Not Write — But Your Guests Will</h2>
          <p class="ht-why__intro">Untreated hotel glass works against your P&amp;L in three directions simultaneously. Your HVAC is fighting solar heat gain that accounts for 25–35% of wasted building energy (U.S. Department of Energy) — and in a hotel, that fight runs 24 hours a day because guests are sleeping in those rooms, not just working in them. Your housekeeping team fields room-move requests from guests on south-facing floors every summer afternoon. And your purchasing department is on a shortened replacement cycle for the carpets, drapery, and upholstery in those same rooms — because UV radiation fades premium furnishings in a fraction of the time they should last.</p>
          <ul class="ht-why__bullets">
            <li>
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M8 12l3 3 5-5" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
              South- and west-facing rooms generate a disproportionate share of comfort complaints on online review platforms — the ones future guests read before booking.
            </li>
            <li>
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M8 12l3 3 5-5" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
              Hotels spend $3,000–$20,000+ per room on furnishings; UV-exposed rooms can require refurnishing every 2–3 years instead of every 7–10.
            </li>
            <li>
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M8 12l3 3 5-5" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
              Guests who close their blackout drapes against afternoon sun never see the city view they paid a premium to access.
            </li>
            <li>
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M8 12l3 3 5-5" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
              Window film addresses all three problems from a single installation — at a fraction of the cost of window replacement.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <div class="ht-why__climate-facts">
            <div class="ht-why__climate-item">
              <span class="ht-why__climate-num">91°F</span>
              <span class="ht-why__climate-label">ASHRAE summer design temp, Philadelphia (Zone 4A)</span>
            </div>
            <div class="ht-why__climate-item">
              <span class="ht-why__climate-num">33%</span>
              <span class="ht-why__climate-label">Of commercial cooling costs from solar heat gain (3M)</span>
            </div>
            <div class="ht-why__climate-item">
              <span class="ht-why__climate-num">16.26¢</span>
              <span class="ht-why__climate-label">Average per kWh electricity rate, Philadelphia (2026)</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <a href="/contact/" class="ht-why__cta">
            Get a free hospitality assessment
            <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M4.5 12h15m0 0l-6.75-6.75M19.5 12l-6.75 6.75"/></svg>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══ HOTEL SPACES GRID ══ -->
    <section class="ht-spaces">
      <div class="ht-spaces__container">
        <div class="ht-spaces__header">
          <span class="ht-spaces__eyebrow">Where We Install</span>
          <h2 class="ht-spaces__headline">The Right Film for Every Part of Your Hotel</h2>
          <p class="ht-spaces__sub">Different spaces in a Philadelphia hotel have different performance requirements. Here's how hotel window film is specified for each area of your property.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ht-spaces__grid">

          <div class="ht-spaces__card">
            <div class="ht-spaces__img-wrap">
              <img src="/images/hotel-space-guest-room.jpg" alt="Philadelphia hotel guest room with solar control window film — comfortable temperature, clear views, no glare" class="ht-spaces__img" loading="lazy" />
            </div>
            <div class="ht-spaces__body">
              <h3 class="ht-spaces__title">Guest Rooms</h3>
              <p class="ht-spaces__desc">South- and west-facing rooms are the biggest problem area in most Philadelphia hotels. Solar control film cuts heat gain by up to 38%, eliminating the hot-room complaints that hurt review scores. UV blocking protects mattresses, drapery, and furniture from premature fading.</p>
              <div class="ht-spaces__tags">
                <span>Solar Control</span><span>UV Protection</span><span>Glare Reduction</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="ht-spaces__card">
            <div class="ht-spaces__img-wrap">
              <img src="/images/hotel-space-lobby.jpg" alt="Philadelphia hotel lobby entrance with professional window film — welcoming natural light, no heat or glare" class="ht-spaces__img" loading="lazy" />
            </div>
            <div class="ht-spaces__body">
              <h3 class="ht-spaces__title">Lobby &amp; Entrance</h3>
              <p class="ht-spaces__desc">Floor-to-ceiling lobby glass makes a dramatic first impression — but it also creates a solar heat and glare problem your HVAC was never designed to handle alone. Solar control film maintains the open, light-filled aesthetic while dramatically reducing cooling demand at check-in peak hours.</p>
              <div class="ht-spaces__tags">
                <span>Solar Control</span><span>Decorative</span><span>Anti-Graffiti</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="ht-spaces__card">
            <div class="ht-spaces__img-wrap">
              <img src="/images/hotel-space-restaurant.jpg" alt="Philadelphia hotel restaurant with window film — comfortable dining, no harsh afternoon glare on tables" class="ht-spaces__img" loading="lazy" />
            </div>
            <div class="ht-spaces__body">
              <h3 class="ht-spaces__title">Restaurant &amp; Bar</h3>
              <p class="ht-spaces__desc">Afternoon dining and happy hour are peak revenue windows — and peak solar intrusion hours. Glare on tables and heat buildup near glass walls creates uncomfortable conditions that guests notice. Solar control and glare-reduction film keeps the atmosphere right without blocking the view your guests came for.</p>
              <div class="ht-spaces__tags">
                <span>Solar Control</span><span>Glare Reduction</span><span>Privacy Film</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="ht-spaces__card">
            <div class="ht-spaces__img-wrap">
              <img src="/images/hotel-space-pool.jpg" alt="Philadelphia hotel pool area with solar and privacy window film — comfortable, private, UV-protected" class="ht-spaces__img" loading="lazy" />
            </div>
            <div class="ht-spaces__body">
              <h3 class="ht-spaces__title">Pool, Spa &amp; Fitness</h3>
              <p class="ht-spaces__desc">Glass-enclosed pool and spa spaces trap heat quickly and create privacy challenges. UV blocking protects guests using the space from cumulative UV exposure. Frosted and decorative film adds privacy for spa treatment rooms and changing areas without making the space feel enclosed.</p>
              <div class="ht-spaces__tags">
