            <p class="ht-row__body">An office can dial down its HVAC at 6pm and recover overnight. A hotel cannot — guest rooms run climate control around the clock. A west-facing room that absorbs solar heat all afternoon is still radiating at 9pm when a guest checks in. The HVAC has been running since noon. Solar control film stops the problem at the glass: 3M Prestige 70 cuts heat gain 38% while maintaining 70% visible light — rooms stay bright, HVAC load drops, and the <a href="https://www.energy.gov/energysaver/energy-efficient-window-attachments" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">DOE-estimated 25–35% of energy</a> lost through inefficient windows starts working in your favor instead of against it.</p>
