            <p class="ht-row__body">Guests who booked a city-view room and paid extra for it expect to enjoy that view. When afternoon sun makes the TV unwatchable and the room uncomfortable, they pull the blackout drapes and don't open them again. "Beautiful views we never got to enjoy" is a real phrase in hotel reviews. <a href="/benefits/glare-reduction/">Glare-reduction window film</a> — like the Vista SpectraSelect VS70 — filters the harsh wavelengths responsible for visual discomfort while maintaining 70% visible light. The room stays open and bright. Guests get the view they paid for. The same film eliminates the afternoon glare that empties your best window tables during peak F&amp;B hours.</p>
