          <div class="ht-ftype__content">
            <div class="ht-ftype__step">01</div>
            <h2 class="ht-ftype__title">Solar Control Film.
Keep Rooms Cool. Cut Energy Costs.</h2>
            <p class="ht-ftype__desc">The south-facing suites that generate "too hot" reviews every summer. Solar control film stops the problem at the glass — blocking heat before it reaches the room so guests experience it the way it was designed to feel. 3M Prestige 70 and Vista SpectraSelect VS70 maintain 70%+ natural light. Guests notice the comfort. They don't notice the film.</p>
            <div class="ht-ftype__faq">
              <div class="ht-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="ht-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Can we prioritize the worst-offending rooms first?<span class="ht-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="ht-ftype__faq-a" hidden>Yes — and we recommend it. Most hotels have a specific exposure or floor range where comfort complaints cluster. We phase the installation to address those rooms first so you see measurable review improvement on the priority inventory before the rest of the property is complete. We coordinate the sequence directly with your front desk and housekeeping team.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="ht-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="ht-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Will motorized shades or blackout curtains still work after film is installed?<span class="ht-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="ht-ftype__faq-a" hidden>Yes — film goes on the glass surface; it does not interact with or affect existing window treatments. In practice, once solar control film is installed, many guests use their blackout curtains only for sleeping rather than as a heat and glare defense, which means they actually get to enjoy the room and view they booked.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="ht-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="ht-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">What is the typical payback period for a Philadelphia hotel?<span class="ht-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="ht-ftype__faq-a" hidden>Most Philadelphia hotels see payback on energy savings alone in 2–4 years, depending on glass area, orientation, and current electricity rate. When you add furnishing lifecycle extension — slowing the replacement cycle in sun-facing rooms — the combined return is typically faster. We provide a basic savings estimate as part of the site assessment at no charge.</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <a href="/contact/" class="ht-ftype__cta">Get a solar control estimate &#x2192;</a>
          </div>
