        <!-- SLIDE 02: Privacy / Frosted -->
        <div class="ht-ftype__slide" data-slide="1">
          <img src="/images/hotel-slider-privacy.jpg" alt="Frosted privacy window film in Philadelphia hotel spa — diffused natural light, guest privacy maintained" class="ht-ftype__bg" />
          <div class="ht-ftype__overlay"></div>
          <div class="ht-ftype__content">
            <div class="ht-ftype__step">02</div>
            <h2 class="ht-ftype__title">Privacy Film.
Frosted. One-Way Mirror. Custom.</h2>
            <p class="ht-ftype__desc">Frosted film provides all-day, all-night privacy for spa treatment rooms, changing areas, and ground-floor rooms on busy street corridors. One-way mirror film provides daytime privacy from outside while preserving outward views for guests inside. Decorative frosted patterns can match your brand aesthetic or complement historic architectural details.</p>
            <div class="ht-ftype__faq">
              <div class="ht-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="ht-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Does one-way mirror work at night?<span class="ht-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="ht-ftype__faq-a" hidden>One-way mirror film relies on a brightness differential — it's private from outside during daylight when exterior is brighter than interior. At night with interior lights on, the effect reverses. For rooms that need guaranteed nighttime privacy (spa rooms, ground-floor bedrooms), frosted film is the correct choice.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="ht-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="ht-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Can guests still see the city view through frosted film?<span class="ht-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="ht-ftype__faq-a" hidden>Frosted film diffuses light — guests can perceive light levels and movement but not clear visual detail through the glass. For rooms where the view is a selling point, we typically recommend frosted film on lower panels only (below eye level), with clear or solar control film on the upper portion. This keeps the view intact while adding privacy from passersby at street level.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="ht-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="ht-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Can you match existing frosted glass patterns in our hotel?<span class="ht-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="ht-ftype__faq-a" hidden>3M FASARA offers 100+ decorative patterns in frosted, etched, and textured finishes that can match or complement existing architectural glass throughout a property. We can also produce custom-cut patterns. This is commonly used for branded lobby glass, spa entrance panels, and elevator surrounds.</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <a href="/contact/" class="ht-ftype__cta">Explore privacy film options →</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- SLIDE 03: Security -->
        <div class="ht-ftype__slide" data-slide="2">
          <img src="/images/hotel-slider-security.jpg" alt="Security window film on Philadelphia hotel lobby entrance glass — clear, impact-resistant protection" class="ht-ftype__bg" />
          <div class="ht-ftype__overlay"></div>
          <div class="ht-ftype__content">
            <div class="ht-ftype__step">03</div>
            <h2 class="ht-ftype__title">Security Film.
Hold Glass Together When It Matters.</h2>
            <p class="ht-ftype__desc">Security window film holds shattered glass in the frame on impact — dramatically reducing injury from flying fragments and slowing forced entry. The 3M ScotchShield Ultra S800 (8-mil micro-layered film) is certified to ANSI Z97.1 safety glazing standards and ASTM F1642. For Philadelphia hotels, it's most commonly applied to ground-floor guest room windows, lobby entrance glass, and stairwell glazing.</p>
            <div class="ht-ftype__faq">
              <div class="ht-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="ht-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Does security film change how the glass looks?<span class="ht-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="ht-ftype__faq-a" hidden>Security film is optically clear — it's virtually invisible when installed. Unlike frosted or solar control film, it doesn't add any visible tint, color, or reflectivity. Guests won't know it's there; they'll only benefit from it in the unlikely event of glass breakage.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="ht-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="ht-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Does it qualify for an insurance reduction?<span class="ht-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="ht-ftype__faq-a" hidden>Some commercial property insurers offer premium reductions for documented security glazing upgrades. We provide written documentation of the film type, certification standard met, installation date, and square footage for your risk management records. Check with your broker — the documentation we provide is typically what they need to evaluate eligibility.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="ht-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="ht-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Is 3M Impact Protection Attachment Sealant required?<span class="ht-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="ht-ftype__faq-a" hidden>For blast mitigation and windstorm applications, 3M ScotchShield Ultra series requires IPA (Impact Protection Attachment) Sealant along the window frame perimeter. For standard urban security applications (break-in deterrence, accident protection), film alone provides significant benefit. We assess your application and recommend the appropriate specification.</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <a href="/contact/" class="ht-ftype__cta">Get a security film assessment →</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- SLIDE 04: Decorative -->
        <div class="ht-ftype__slide" data-slide="3">
          <img src="/images/hotel-slider-decorative.jpg" alt="Custom decorative window film in Philadelphia hotel lobby — elegant frosted glass partition panels" class="ht-ftype__bg" />
          <div class="ht-ftype__overlay"></div>
          <div class="ht-ftype__content">
            <div class="ht-ftype__step">04</div>
            <h2 class="ht-ftype__title">Decorative Film.
Brand the Glass. Elevate the Space.</h2>
            <p class="ht-ftype__desc">Lobby partitions, spa entrance panels, restaurant dividers, and elevator surrounds are all opportunities to reinforce your hotel's aesthetic. 3M FASARA and custom-cut decorative films turn plain glass into designed elements — no etching, no permanent modification, and fully removable when you renovate or rebrand.</p>
            <div class="ht-ftype__faq">
              <div class="ht-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="ht-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Can you replicate our hotel brand or logo in window film?<span class="ht-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="ht-ftype__faq-a" hidden>Yes — custom-cut decorative film is produced from vector files, brand guidelines, or architect drawings and cut to exact specifications. Logo marks, proprietary patterns, and architectural motifs are all achievable. Lead time for custom work is typically 2–3 weeks. Standard 3M FASARA patterns (100+ options) are available for rapid installation with no custom lead time.</div>
