              <div class="ht-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="ht-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Is decorative film removable when we renovate or rebrand?<span class="ht-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="ht-ftype__faq-a" hidden>Yes — and this is one of its primary advantages over etched or sandblasted glass. Decorative film can be removed cleanly without affecting the underlying glass. During a property renovation or brand refresh, film removal and re-installation is straightforward and does not require a glazing contractor. This makes it significantly more practical for properties on a 5–7 year renovation cycle.</div>
