            <div class="ht-ftype__step">05</div>
            <h2 class="ht-ftype__title">Anti-Graffiti Film.
Sacrificial Layer. Instant Recovery.</h2>
            <p class="ht-ftype__desc">Anti-graffiti film is a clear sacrificial layer applied to exterior glass surfaces — lobby entrances, street-level windows, mirrors, and elevator interiors. When scratched, etched, or tagged, you remove and replace only the film — not the glass. Replacement costs a fraction of new glass. Common in Center City Philadelphia hotels along Market and Chestnut streets.</p>
            <div class="ht-ftype__faq">
              <div class="ht-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="ht-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">How long does film replacement take after vandalism?<span class="ht-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="ht-ftype__faq-a" hidden>Anti-graffiti film replacement is typically a same-day or next-day service for existing clients. We keep stock of common sizes and can dispatch a technician quickly. Removal and re-application takes 30–60 minutes per panel depending on size — dramatically faster than waiting for glass replacement.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="ht-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="ht-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Can it be used on interior mirrors?<span class="ht-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="ht-ftype__faq-a" hidden>Yes — anti-graffiti film is commonly applied to hotel elevator mirrors, lobby mirror panels, and bathroom mirrors in high-traffic areas. It's optically clear and does not affect the mirror's reflective quality. The cost savings on mirror replacement versus film replacement are significant in elevator applications where scratching is frequent.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="ht-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="ht-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Does it only work on flat glass?<span class="ht-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="ht-ftype__faq-a" hidden>Anti-graffiti film is designed for flat and slightly curved glass surfaces. It cannot be applied to heavily textured or highly curved surfaces. For most hotel lobby glass, elevator panels, and street-level windows, standard flat application works perfectly. We assess the surface during the site visit and confirm compatibility before quoting.</div>
